a10fb41a\nTest input (12x8):\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 7 7 7 7 9 7 7\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 3 2 8 6 7 7 7\n7 2 6 3 7 7 7 7\n7 2 8 2 7 3 7 7\n7 8 7 3 8 8 7 7\n7 7 2 8 8 2 7 7\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\nWrong attempts used: 0/8. Demo requests used: 1/8.\nReply with exactly one action JSON on the last line.","reply":"```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    h, w = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    bg = max(set(x for row in grid for x in row), key=lambda c: sum(row.count(c) for row in grid))\n    pts = [(r, c) for r in range(h) for c in range(w) if grid[r][c] != bg]\n    marker_color = min(set(grid[r][c] for r, c in pts),\n                       key=lambda c: sum(grid[r][c] == c for r, c in pts))\n    markers = [(r, c) for r, c in pts if grid[r][c] == marker_color]\n    shape = [(r, c, grid[r][c]) for r, c in pts if grid[r][c] != marker_color]\n    if not markers or not shape:\n        return grid\n    r0 = min(r for r, c, v in shape)\n    c0 = min(c for r, c, v in shape)\n    r1 = max(r for r, c, v in shape)\n    c1 = max(c for r, c, v in shape)\n    ar, ac = (r0 + r1) // 2, (c0 + c1) // 2\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    for r, c in markers:\n        out[r][c] = bg\n        dr, dc = r - ar, c - ac\n        for sr, sc, v in shape:\n            rr, cc = sr + dr, sc + dc\n            if 0 <= rr < h and 0 <= cc < w:\n                out[rr][cc] = v\n    return out\n```\n{\"action\":\"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit"}},{"step":175,"kind":"reprompt","phase":"act","t0":1790712545.517,"t1":1790712557.267,"alias":"task-a10fb41a","message":"Your program was checked on demo pair 1 at no cost and its output is wrong. It gave\n3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3\n3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3\n3 3 2 4 9 2 6 3 3 3 3 3 6 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3\n3 3 7 8 9 5 8 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 6 3 3 3 3 3 3 3\n3 3 3 9 8 3 5 3 3 3 3 6 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3\n3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 