ly":"```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    h, w = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    from collections import Counter\n    counts = Counter(v for row in grid for v in row)\n    bg = counts.most_common(1)[0][0]\n    cells = [(r, c, grid[r][c]) for r in range(h) for c in range(w)\n             if grid[r][c] != bg]\n\n    # The single rare-color cell is the placement marker.\n    freq = Counter(v for r, c, v in cells)\n    marker_color = min(freq, key=freq.get)\n    markers = [(r, c) for r, c, v in cells if v == marker_color]\n    shape_cells = [(r, c, v) for r, c, v in cells if v != marker_color]\n    r0 = min(r for r, c, v in shape_cells)\n    r1 = max(r for r, c, v in shape_cells)\n    c0 = min(c for r, c, v in shape_cells)\n    c1 = max(c for r, c, v in shape_cells)\n    shape = [(r-r0, c-c0, v) for r, c, v in shape_cells]\n\n    # Markers align with the center cell of the pattern's bounding box.\n    ar, ac = (r1-r0)//2, (c1-c0)//2\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    for r, c in markers:\n        out[r][c] = bg\n        top, left = r-ar, c-ac\n        for dr, dc, v in shape:\n            rr, cc = top+dr, left+dc\n            if 0 <= rr < h and 0 <= cc < w:\n                out[rr][cc] = v\n    return out\n```\n{\"action\":\"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit"}},{"step":175,"kind":"reprompt","phase":"act","t0":1790712577.096,"t1":1790712588.256,"alias":"task-a10fb41a","message":"Your program was checked on demo pair 1 at no cost and its output is wrong. It gave\n3 3 3 3 3 3 3 6 3 3 3 3 3 6 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3\n3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3\n3 3 2 3 9 2 2 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3\n6 3 7 8 9 5 8 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 6 3 3 3 3 3 3 3\n3 3 0 9 8 3 5 3 6 3 3 6 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3\n3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 6 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3\n3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3\n3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3\n3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 6 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 6